import{_ as e,o as t,c as a,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 553 | Dual-Track Time Domain | Evolution of Civilizational Weight in the Time Domain","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 553 | Dual-Track Time Domain | Evolution of Civilizational Weight in the Time Domain","no":553,"module":3,"tags":["Dual-Track Time Domain","Civilizational Weight","Evolution","Joint Contracting","Ascension"],"related":["29-Symbiotic-Degree Evaluation System","22-Joint-Contracting Resource-Distribution Mechanism","17-Plane-Transcendent Strongest Standard","05-Myriad-Ranks Joint-Advancement Basic Program"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0553_模块3-双轨时间域-时间域中的文明权重演化.md","filePath":"en/0553_模块3-双轨时间域-时间域中的文明权重演化.md"}'),n={name:"en/0553_模块3-双轨时间域-时间域中的文明权重演化.md"};function r(s,i,l,h,u,c){return t(),a("div",null,[...i[0]||(i[0]=[o('<h1 id="entry-553-dual-track-time-domain-evolution-of-civilizational-weight-in-the-time-domain" tabindex="-1">Entry 553 | Dual-Track Time Domain | Evolution of Civilizational Weight in the Time Domain <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-553-dual-track-time-domain-evolution-of-civilizational-weight-in-the-time-domain" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 553 | Dual-Track Time Domain | Evolution of Civilizational Weight in the Time Domain&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 3 · Dual-Track Time Domain Civilizational-Experience System | Benchmark base: Documents 29, 22, 17, 05</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-in-dual-track-time-how-a-civilization-s-weight-gets-a-little-heavier" tabindex="-1">Introduction: in dual-track time, how a civilization&#39;s &quot;weight&quot; gets a little heavier <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-in-dual-track-time-how-a-civilization-s-weight-gets-a-little-heavier" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: in dual-track time, how a civilization&#39;s &quot;weight&quot; gets a little heavier&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Civilizational weight is a comprehensive metric measuring a civilization in Myriad-Rank Republicanism: &quot;how much say it has, how much responsibility it bears, how much acceleration resource it gets.&quot; It is not born fated, but <strong>evolved little by little</strong> in the time domain. What this entry covers is how the dual-track time domain&#39;s mechanism makes civilizational weight rise and fall with co-building contribution — it rewards &quot;lifting Myriad Ranks,&quot; not &quot;crushing Myriad Ranks.&quot;</p><p>Six top-level axioms run through: anti-predation axiom requires weight not accumulated by predation; republican axiom of Myriad Races requires weight open to all civilizations, everyone can rise; collective ascension axiom directly links weight evolution to &quot;lifting all&quot;; causal self-discipline axiom requires weight rises and leaves auditable traces throughout; law-first axiom requires weight rules defined first by law, not by personal likes and dislikes. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-what-civilizational-weight-evolves-by" tabindex="-1">I. What Civilizational Weight Evolves By <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-what-civilizational-weight-evolves-by" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. What Civilizational Weight Evolves By&quot;">​</a></h2><p>After sandbox dissection, civilizational weight mainly accumulates from three types of contribution:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Contribution Type</th><th>Source</th><th>Corresponding Weight Gain</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Co-Building Output</td><td>Produce shareable techniques, methods, proposals in the acceleration domain</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>Correction Contribution</td><td>Complete reviews in the Quest Domain; help reversing civilizations recover</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>Myriad-Rank Lifting</td><td>Lift own race and surrounding beings&#39; evolutionary level</td><td>Medium-High</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Note: none of the three contribution types is linked to &quot;combat power&quot; or &quot;predation amount.&quot; A civilization even if extremely strong in combat, if only used to predate, weight falls rather than rises — because predation itself is deducted. This is in the same line as Plane-Transcendent four-dimensional assessment (Power 40 / Mind 25 / Contribution 20 / Responsibility 15): contribution and responsibility account for half; power only four-tenths.</p><h2 id="ii-dual-track-division-of-labor-for-weight-evolution" tabindex="-1">II. Dual-Track Division of Labor for Weight Evolution <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-dual-track-division-of-labor-for-weight-evolution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Dual-Track Division of Labor for Weight Evolution&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The dual-track time domain precisely divides labor for weight&#39;s two dimensions:</p><ul><li><strong>Origin Acceleration Domain</strong> handles &quot;hard-contribution weight&quot;: the more output, the more shareable, the faster weight rises; this is the weight civilization &quot;earns by working&quot; in time.</li><li><strong>Quest Sediment Domain</strong> handles &quot;soft-contribution weight&quot;: the deeper the review, the more corrections, the more solid the lifting, the steadier weight rises; this is the weight civilization &quot;sediments&quot; in time.</li></ul><p>Only hard contribution without soft contribution, weight is &quot;falsely high&quot; — in the sandbox such civilization shows its weakness once it encounters crisis; only soft contribution without hard contribution, weight is &quot;falsely low&quot; — willing but unable, can&#39;t help Myriad Ranks. <strong>Dual tracks combined, weight is real.</strong></p><h2 id="iii-weight-rise-and-fall-why-there-must-be-a-fall" tabindex="-1">III. Weight Rise and Fall: Why There Must Be a &quot;Fall&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-weight-rise-and-fall-why-there-must-be-a-fall" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Weight Rise and Fall: Why There Must Be a &quot;Fall&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Many civilizational mechanisms only reward rise, not punish fall; result: weight decoupled from real contribution, degenerating into a title. The Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s weight evolution is <strong>two-way</strong>:</p><ul><li>Predation signs, knowledge secret-hoarding, reversal relapse appear; weight lowered per rules;</li><li>Weight lowered means callable acceleration resources, decision-making say shrink synchronously;</li><li>Severe cases, after Symbiotic Court adjudication, freeze their law-anchoring permissions.</li></ul><p>The two-way mechanism guarantees weight always clings to real contribution, and will not solidify into new class privilege — this is precisely the institutional immunity against &quot;class stratification&quot; reversal.</p><h2 id="iv-weight-evolution-and-the-closed-loop-of-myriad-rank-republicanism" tabindex="-1">IV. Weight Evolution and the Closed Loop of Myriad-Rank Republicanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-weight-evolution-and-the-closed-loop-of-myriad-rank-republicanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Weight Evolution and the Closed Loop of Myriad-Rank Republicanism&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Weight evolution ultimately serves Myriad-Rank Republicanism: the higher the weight, the more responsibility Myriad Ranks entrust to that civilization, the more acceleration resources it can call, but <strong>these resources must continue to be used to lift Myriad Ranks</strong>, not enjoyed alone. Thus a healthy closed loop forms: co-build → weight rises → get more acceleration resources → larger-scale co-building → weight rises again. In this loop, &quot;getting stronger&quot; and &quot;making Myriad Ranks better&quot; are the same thing — this is precisely the collective ascension axiom&#39;s perfect closed loop in the time dimension.</p><p>In the sandbox there once appeared a &quot;falsely high weight&quot; counterexample: a civilization in the short term rushed to a high weight through one high-intensity R&amp;D sprint, but long-term did not return knowledge or lift; weight then per rules fell month by month. This fall did not trigger dissatisfaction; instead ethnic groups saw it as fair — because it proved weight is &quot;earned, guarded,&quot; not a once-and-for-all title. The two-way mechanism keeps weight always flowing with real contribution, not solidifying into new classes.</p><h2 id="v-weight-s-public-transparency-to-myriad-ranks" tabindex="-1">V. Weight&#39;s Public Transparency to Myriad Ranks <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-weight-s-public-transparency-to-myriad-ranks" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Weight&#39;s Public Transparency to Myriad Ranks&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Weight&#39;s entire calculation process is public to Myriad Ranks: why a civilization&#39;s weight rises, why it falls, which contribution was scored, which violation deducted, anyone may query. This transparency itself is constraint — no one dares hoard in the open, because once hoarding is recorded in the public ledger, the deduction far exceeds what was embezzled. Thus weight is not just a ranking; it becomes Myriad Ranks&#39; jointly supervised dashboard of civilizational direction. Civilization therefore need not worry about &quot;being secretly scored in a black box,&quot; because every point is laid in the sun.</p><h2 id="vi-weight-is-not-the-endpoint" tabindex="-1">VI. Weight Is Not the Endpoint <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-weight-is-not-the-endpoint" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Weight Is Not the Endpoint&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Finally to emphasize: weight no matter how high, is only proof of &quot;entrusted with more,&quot; not capital to lie back and enjoy. The highest-weight civilization precisely bears the heaviest lifting responsibility. Thus this mechanism naturally repels the &quot;once reaching the top, retire&quot; mentality — the higher the weight, the more you must move forward. This is precisely its fundamental divergence from Tang Luo&#39;s &quot;reaching the top means eternity.&quot;</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: weight follows co-building output, precisely investing acceleration resources in the civilizations best able to lift Myriad Ranks, avoiding resource misallocation</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: predation not scored but deducted, structurally making &quot;grabbing&quot; a losing deal in the weight economy</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo&#39;s &quot;weight&quot; distributed by fists and bounty; Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s civilizational weight evolved little by little through dual-track co-building</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: weight rises and falls open to all civilizations equally; weak civilizations as long as truly co-build, weight can also rise</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: three types of contribution accounting, two-way rise-and-fall rules, four-dimensional assessment standards all public, self-checkable, appealable</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Civilizational weight evolution in the time domain wrests &quot;civilizational status&quot; from bloodline, fists, bounty, and hands it to &quot;co-building contribution&quot; itself. In dual-track time, a civilization need not crush others to get heavier — it only needs to honestly produce on the fast track, sediment on the slow track, lift Myriad Ranks little by little, and its weight naturally grows day by day. This kind of weight rises slowly, but cannot be crushed.</p><p>In the final analysis, civilizational weight evolution in the time domain described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./29-共生度评估体系.html">29-Symbiotic-Degree Evaluation System</a> · <a href="./22-资源分配联产承包机制.html">22-Joint-Contracting Resource-Distribution Mechanism</a> · <a href="./17-位面至高强者标准.html">17-Plane-Transcendent Strongest Standard</a> · <a href="./05-万族共进基本纲领.html">05-Myriad-Ranks Joint-Advancement Basic Program</a></li></ul>',31)])])}const m=e(n,[["render",r]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
